<title>USA: Lam to buy OnTrak, sees Q3 loss.</title>
<headline>Lam to buy OnTrak, sees Q3 loss.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lam Research Corp, expanding its expertise in semiconductor manufacturing equipment, said Monday it agreed to buy OnTrak Systems Inc for $225 million in stock.</p>
<p>Lam Research, a manufacturer of computer chipmaking equipment, also said it expects to report a loss of $1.40 a share for the fiscal third quarter because of a $10-$15 million shortfall and a write-down of old inventory.</p>
<p>Wall Street was expecting a profit of $0.07 for the third quarter ending March 31.</p>
</text>
